{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now with Date sort, order is Shopping, todo, Notes, Single, Regex, Regex2, Money, Indent, Indent2. All same date 3:07 PM, so tie order might be arbitrary. Hmm, all files have same timestamp it seems. So sorting by date ties. The order appears reversed? Initially Name order ascending: Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo. Note Regex2 before Regex - with Name sort, hmm \"Regex2.md\" vs \"Regex.md\": comparing \"Regex2\" vs \"Regex.\"? '.'=46, '2'=50, so Regex. < Regex2, so Regex.md should come first ascending. It showed Regex2 before Regex... that's a bit odd. Maybe case-insensitive? Or maybe locale collation ignoring punctuation? Hmm.\n\nActually in current Date order it's Shopping, todo, Notes, Single, Regex, Regex2, Money, Indent, Indent2. That is exactly reverse of the name order: name order was [Zeta folder, Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo]. Reverse = [todo, Single, Shopping, Regex, Regex2, Notes, Money, Indent, Indent2]. Current is [Shopping, todo, Notes, Single, Regex, Regex2, Money, Indent, Indent2]. Not exactly reverse.\n\nHmm, actually current order: Shopping, todo, Notes, Single, Regex, Regex2, Money, Indent, Indent2. Reverse of initial (excluding folder): todo, Single, Shopping, Regex, Regex2, Notes, Money, Indent, Indent2. Not matching first three.\n\nMaybe the current order is a stable tie sort from the original insertion order? Hard to say. All items date equal (same second) so date sorting ties. Not a good test for ordering correctness. But the sort choice persistence is the change. Let me verify: reopen sort menu — Date should be checked. Then leave the app / reopen (or go to another tab and come back) and check Date is still checked.\n\nLet me tap sort again."}
