{"type": "thinking", "text": "Bug? Selecting \"Wikitext / Zim\" left the extension as \".txt\" instead of updating to \".wiki\" or \".zim\". Hmm, maybe Wikitext format's extension is \".txt\"? No — Wikitext / Zim files typically use \".wiki\" or \".zim\". Let's check: In Markor, supported formats: Markdown (.md), todo.txt (.txt), Plain Text (.txt), Wikitext (.wiki), AsciiDoc (.adoc), OrgMode (.org), CSV (.csv). The extension list \"built directly from supported formats\" may be a list of extensions offered in the extension dropdown. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the extension only changes when type is selected via spinner and a flag? It changed for Plain Text from \".\" to \".txt\" (maybe since text was \".\" it appended? no, it replaced with \".txt\").\n\nActually when we selected Plain Text, the ext field went from \".\" to \".txt\", so the type selection triggers extension update. Then selecting Wikitext left \".txt\". Maybe Wikitext's default extension IS \".txt\"? Hmm. In Markor, the Format list includes \"Wikitext / Zim\" with extension \".txt\"? Let me recall Markor's `DocumentFormat` enum: MARKDOWN(\"md\"), TEXT(\"txt\"), TODOTXT(\"txt\"), WIKITEXT(\"txt\"), ASCIIDOC(\"adoc\"), ORGMODE(\"org\"), CSV(\"csv\"). Hmm, maybe Wikitext uses \".txt\"? Actually Zim wiki uses .txt files! Zim stores pages as .txt. So .txt might be correct for Wikitext/Zim.\n\nLet's check AsciiDoc next; expect \".adoc\". And OrgMode \".org\", CSV \".csv\", todo.txt \".txt\", Markdown \".md\". Let's test."}
