{"type": "thinking", "text": "Name order: Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo. Same as initial. Note Regex2 before Regex, which seems wrong if sorting lexicographically (Regex.md < Regex2.md). Hmm, let's think: comparing full names \"Regex.md\" and \"Regex2.md\". At char index 5: \"Regex\" then \".\" (46) vs \"2\" (50). \".\" < \"2\" so Regex.md should come first in ASCII. But maybe the comparison is case-insensitive using Collator, which may ignore punctuation? ICU Collator default treats punctuation as significant but may have different ordering: In ICU (locale en), punctuation is \"shifted\" maybe? Default Collator: non-alphanumeric characters sort before digits? Actually UCA: punctuation < digits < letters typically. Hmm.\n\nBut maybe Markor compares file names using `String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER`? Then \"Regex.\" vs \"Regex2\": '.' < '2' still Regex first. So Regex2 before Regex is suspicious. But wait, could it be sorting by display title without extension? Titles \"Regex2\" vs \"Regex\": \"Regex\" < \"Regex2\" (prefix shorter first). So Regex should be first. Hmm.\n\nThis might be a bug in name sorting (natural sort?). But the \"changed\" area is sort choice persistence, not name compare. However, QA sweep should find bugs. But careful: Sorting files with equal dates earlier gave Date order... hmm.\n\nActually wait: compare with names sorted case-sensitively ignoring extension? \"Indent2.md\" vs \"Indent.md\": '2'(50) < '.'(46)? No, '.'=46 < '2'=50, so \"Indent.md\" should come first by ASCII. But observed Indent2 before Indent. So the comparator appears to ignore the '.' extension separator, comparing base names: \"Indent\" < \"Indent2\" → Indent first... but observed Indent2 first! That contradicts.\n\nHmm, let's list observed: Indent2, Indent, Money, Notes, Regex2, Regex, Shopping, Single, todo.\n\nWait \"todo.txt\" at end. Compare base names: Indent, Indent2, Money, Notes, Regex, Regex2, Shopping, Single, todo. Descending base order? No: Indent2, Indent is descending among those two; Regex2, Regex is descending; Money, Notes ascending; Shopping, Single: \"Shopping\" vs \"Single\": 'h' vs 'i' → Shopping < Single ascending. todo last: 't' after 'S' if case-insensitive? \"todo\" vs \"Shopping\": t > s, so should come after Shopping/Single — yes ascending. So it's inconsistent for pairs where one name is prefix of another: the longer \"Indent2\" sorts before \"Indent\". That suggests comparison is done in a way where \"Indent2.md\" < \"Indent.md\". How? If comparing full filenames case-insensitively and using a natural/collation that ignores punctuation, \"Indent2md\" vs \"Indentmd\": '2'(digit) < 'm'(letter) → Indent2md first! Yes! ICU collation: digits sort before letters. So \"Regex2md\" vs \"Regexmd\": '2' < 'm' → Regex2 first. That explains it. So it's a locale collation where digits < letters, punctuation maybe ignored. That's plausible normal behavior. Not a bug.\n\nOK.\n\nNow test Reverse order toggle. Open sort dialog, check Reverse order, OK, see reversed order. Then leave & re-open to verify persistence. Then restore."}
