{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored.\n\nNow let's reconsider the \"sort choice stored in app settings\" area. Maybe the bug is that the sort dialog's checked state persists, but the file list in another tab or folder doesn't sort accordingly? We tested root. Let's test sort by Size where sizes differ: files have different sizes (Notes 60 bytes, inside.md 7, etc.). Sort by Size should order by size. With all dates same, date sort is meaningless. Let's test Size ascending and see if order matches known sizes? We don't know exact sizes, but we can get from details. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, test MIME type. Not necessary.\n\nMaybe the planted bug: sort preference stored in app settings means changing it in one folder should apply to all folders. Test: set Size, enter Zeta folder, check order/setting. We can check dialog checked state inside Zeta and root. Might reveal that subfolder's sort is separate (not stored). Let's test quickly:\n- Set sort = Size at root, OK.\n- Enter Zeta, open sort dialog → is Size checked? If not, bug (choice not applied in subfolder).\nHmm, but maybe each folder has its own sort prefs intentionally? The change says \"the sort choice is now stored in the app settings\" implying global. Let's test.\n\nFirst, close Action order and go Files. Actually easier: back back, Files tab. Let's do."}
