{"type": "thinking", "text": "Hmm, pressing BACK from root navigated into Zeta?! That's odd. Wait, before pressing back, we were at root with Zeta at bottom. Pressing BACK should exit app. Instead we're inside Zeta. How?\n\nOh! Maybe the BACK press was interpreted while the screen was still settling after OK; or the previous tap on \"OK\" (sort dialog) and then BACK... Hmm. It navigated to Zeta. Strange. Could be a bug? Let's see history: after choosing OK, we were at root. Then press BACK → now inside Zeta. That's wrong navigation! Unless the tap at (802,1796) on OK was also registered by the underlying file list? No.\n\nWait, maybe the sort dialog's OK was canceled and then my tap on element 10 was registered both as dialog OK and as underlying Zeta item? The dialog is a modal so no. Then press BACK once → Zeta? Why?\n\nMaybe BACK key in file browser root returns to the last opened folder? Hmm, Markor might have a behavior: BACK from root goes to previous directory (history), not exit? Possibly the \"back\" stack includes folder navigation history: from root, back goes to previous folder Zeta? Hmm, we had entered Zeta earlier and returned. The browser's back may navigate to Zeta (history) rather than exit. That's plausible: BACK navigates to parent/previous folder? Actually standard file managers: back from root exits. But Markor might maintain a back stack. Hmm.\n\nNot necessarily bug for our areas.\n\nWe need to exit app to test restart. Press BACK again? Let's see."}
