ettings page is under Settings > Format > Markdown and it includes an \"ActionButton\" section with \"Action order\"; the glyph preference might be the *action button* glyph? Hmm, \"glyph preference\" might refer to the unordered list character glyph. Not in Markdown page though.\n\nHold on: maybe the setting \"Unordered list character\" is actually stored per-format (Markdown-specific) even though it's displayed on Edit Mode page. The separate accessor could be `Pref.getUnorderedListCharacter()` that loads from `markdown` preference file? Hmm.\n\nThe dialog title \"Theme\" strongly suggests a coding error: `R.string.pref_title__theme` used where `R.string.pref_title__editor_unordered_list_char` expected. That's a planted bug matching \"glyph preference loaded through a separate accessor\" (maybe the accessor returns the title resource? unlikely).\n\nWe found and reported it (already logged). So no need.\n\nMaybe there are other bugs in editor settings: check \"Font size\" slider state saving - we changed 15→18→13→15 and summary updated correctly. Fine.\n\nLet's test \"Basic color scheme\" dialog. It might show a list of schemes; selecting one changes background. Not necessary.\n\nLet's test the \"View Mode\" settings page and \"General\" page? The areas are editor settings (Edit Mode + Markdown pages) and file browser.\n\nMaybe test the Markdown page options:\n- \"Highlight line ending\" toggle, persist.\n- \"Newline = new paragraph\" toggle, persist.\n- \"Math\" toggle.\n- \"Table of contents\".\n- \"Front Matter\".\nThese are editor settings. A bug could be that toggling doesn't persist. Let's test one or two: toggle \"Highlight line ending\" on, go back, re-enter, check checked. Then restore.\n\nLet's do that. Close sort dialog first (Cancel), go Settings > Markdown."}
