{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now let's think about the file browser \"new-file dialog extension list\" more: maybe the bug is that the extension list (AutoComplete suggestions) is missing or wrong for some format. The dev couldn't reproduce the todo thing, so maybe the intended bug is different. Let's inspect the extension field's autocomplete list by examining the accessibility tree when the dropdown shows. Perhaps need to tap the small arrow? The field is just EditText though. Maybe long-press brings \"Paste\"? Hmm.\n\nMaybe the extension list is displayed in the *hint* when the field is empty: \".md ...\" — perhaps it should list all supported extensions but is truncated due to a bug in how it's built (e.g., join with \" ... \"?). Let's clear the field and observe the full hint in the element text: \".md ...\". So hint = \".md ...\". Could be intended hint \"e.g. .md\" but weird.\n\nWait, maybe the hint is generated by `TextUtils.join(\" \", DocumentFormat.values())` and the result is \".md ...\" because the list contains \".md\" then \"...\"? Hmm.\n\nLet's look at the empty extension field hint in these observations: after clear, element text \".md ...\". Maybe it's not hint; maybe the app has an AutoCompleteTextView whose adapter list is set and `setText` to first item? Then the field might show the first suggestion plus \"...\"? Hmm.\n\nMaybe the extension field is an AutoCompleteTextView with entries [\".md\", ...] and `setCompletionHint`? No.\n\nI think the hint is just examples. Move on.\n\nLet's test new-file dialog with \"Folder\" button: creates a folder. We shouldn't pollute; can create then delete. But maybe a bug: FOLDER button with extension present creates folder named with extension? The info says \"Folder is created without file extension\". Test: type name \"QATemp\", ext \".md\", tap FOLDER → should create folder \"QATemp\" (no ext). Then delete it. That's a data change but testing requires; we can cleanup.\n\nAlso test \"Template\" spinner options: e.g., for Markdown, templates like \"Empty file\", \"Meeting\", \"Diary\"? Selecting template populates content? Could test.\n\nBut we should prioritize likely planted bugs. Let's recall the changed bullets:\n1. Sort menu choice stored in app settings. — We tested persistence thoroughly; no bug found. Maybe the bug is the independent \"Folder local\" behavior? Hmm.\n2. Markdown section glyph preference separate accessor. — Bugs found (title + action), already logged.\n3. Unordered list action detects existing list markers new way. — Bug found (indented marker duplicate), confirmed/logged.\n4. New-file dialog extension list built from supported formats. — Our .todo.txt finding rejected (\"could not reproduce\"). Maybe there's another bug: e.g., the extension list includes \".md\" always? Or the extension field not updating when choosing type (we saw it updates). Hmm, maybe the actual bug is that choosing a type sets the extension but choosing \"Markdown\" after a custom extension resets it, overriding user's custom extension. That could be the \"extension list built directly from supported formats\" bug: the type's extension mapping uses a list of formats and overwrites user-typed extension. But this is standard.\n\nWait, maybe the intended behavior: the extension field has an AutoComplete list of ALL extensions from supported formats, so the user can choose any extension. The bug: the list is built incorrectly (e.g., using type names instead of extensions), so the AutoComplete suggestions are \".Markdown\", \".Plain Text\", \".todo.txt\", etc. Our observed type→extension behavior could be driven by that list: when selecting Type=todo.txt, it autocompletes to the first list entry matching the type name? Hmm.\n\nMaybe we should trigger the autocomplete dropdown to see the extension list. In an AutoCompleteTextView, typing may show suggestions after a threshold. Our typing \"t\" in the ext field did not show; but maybe because the field's adapter is set only after dialog opens and the keyboard's suggestions strip? Hmm.\n\nCould the extension field be a `Spinner`? Observation shows EditText class but with Activity? The element id `new_file_dialog__ext` and hint \".md ...\". In Markor source, the new file dialog has an `AutoCompleteTextView` for extension with `entries` from `R.array.new_file_extension_list`? Actually I recall Markor's \"New file\" dialog has an extension EditText with a dropdown of extensions. Hmm.\n\nLet's try pressing DPAD_DOWN while the ext field is focused and text empty; that might open the dropdown list. We'll see if new elements appear. Test: open FAB, focus ext, clear text (hint shows), press DPAD_DOWN, observe. Let's do."}
