{"type": "thinking", "text": "Wait — \"Folder local\" is checked now, even though we canceled the dialog earlier. Did our earlier OK with Folder local checked persist it? Let's reconstruct: Earlier we selected Folder local while Size checked, then tapped Size (no change), then Name (Folder local + Name), then tapped Folder local again (Folder local unchecked, Size checked), then Date (only Date), then Folder local (Folder local + Date), then CANCEL (discard). So after cancel, state should be Size from before, with Folder local unchecked. But now the dialog shows Folder local checked + Size checked. So CANCEL did NOT discard the Folder local change! Interesting — this indicates \"Folder local\" preference is applied immediately on tap (saved to settings) even before OK/Cancel, while the criterion (Size) is saved on OK. That's a real behavior difference: toggling \"Folder local\" is applied immediately even when the dialog is cancelled.\n\nWait, how did Folder local become checked? In the last dialog sequence, we tapped Folder local to check it (with Date checked), then Cancel. So the Folder local check got persisted despite Cancel. Then opening now shows Folder local checked + Size (the saved criterion before the dialog). This means \"Folder local\" is not treated as part of the dialog's pending choice; it's applied immediately. Is that a bug? It's inconsistent with Cancel semantics: cancel should discard all changes. The other options (Date) were discarded. So Folder local escaped. This is a real bug in sort menu reversal! The task says test \"Reversal: cancel or reverse a change, and check the app returns to the right state.\"\n\nThis is a strong bug candidate! But is \"Folder local\" a separate setting that applies instantly by design? In a dialog with CANCEL/OK, all choices should be applied only on OK. If tapping Folder local immediately changes a preference, then Cancel doesn't cancel it. Also, if it's an independent setting, it should still be subject to OK/Cancel. So bug.\n\nBut wait, maybe the \"Folder local\" row is not part of the dialog's list at all: maybe it's handled by a separate preference and the single-choice dialog rebuilds state from prefs. But visually it's an item in the same list. Tapping it should still not persist on Cancel.\n\nLet's reproduce cleanly and document:\n- Open Sort by. Note current: Folder local checked, Size checked (persisted from our cancel).\n- Uncheck Folder local (tap it) → maybe changes radio? Earlier tapping Folder local when checked resulted in Size checked and Folder local unchecked (the radio remained Size... wait at that time Name was checked; after tap, Size became checked). Hmm, that's weird. Tapping Folder local triggers radio to change to Size? Let me test again now.\n\nLet's carefully record state transitions and Cancel/OK behavior.\n\nCurrent: Folder local checked, Size checked.\nTap CANCEL first to close. Then reopen to confirm same state (it's persisted).\n\nThen:\nStep 1: open dialog, uncheck Folder local by tapping it. Observe state.\nStep 2: tap CANCEL. Reopen. Check if Folder local remained unchecked or was restored to checked.\n\nLet's do. First cancel [9]."}
