om Date to Size? Maybe because the tap on Folder local wasn't a simple toggle; it triggered the app to refresh the sort dialog based on the stored sort method. The user's pending Date selection was lost. If the user then taps OK, they'd get Size instead of Date. That's a real bug: choosing Date then toggling Folder local then OK applies Size. Hmm, but is it reproducible with OK? Let's test:\n\nSequence:\n1. Current state: Folder local checked + Size checked (stored Size).\n2. Tap Date (pending Date).\n3. Tap Folder local (uncheck; radio resets to Size).\n4. Tap OK.\n5. Check order → if Size order, Date choice was lost.\n\nBut the user might not expect toggling Folder local to cancel their Date choice; it's a subtle bug.\n\nAlternatively, maybe tapping Folder local does NOT reset the radio; maybe the radio was already Size because our earlier tap on Date while Folder local checked didn't actually change the pending state? We observed Date checked immediately after tapping Date, so it did. Then tapping Folder local changed the display to Size. So yes it reset.\n\nHmm, but the whole \"Folder local\" behavior is strange. Could be an artifact of the dialog using `setSingleChoiceItems` plus a separate checkbox whose click triggers `sortDialog.show()` recreation? If it re-creates the dialog, the pending state resets. That's a UI bug.\n\nI'm inclined to report this as a sort-dialog state/reset bug. But is it within the changed area? Yes, sort menu.\n\nHowever, the developer might consider it minor/by design. The task expects us to find remaining bugs; we've already found one confirmed new bug (indented marker). We should keep going and maybe find more definite ones.\n\nLet's restore default sort state: Name + Folder first + Folder local? Hmm, what's the app default? Initially (at session start) sort was Name, Folder first checked, Folder local unchecked, Reverse off, .dotfiles off. So restore Folder local unchecked, Name checked, Folder first checked. Currently Folder local